⍝ Parentheses.tc
⍝ ----------------------------------

⍝@ test3.

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs28 #61, 2026-08-11): "( )" with
      ⍝ nothing between the parentheses raised a raw SYNTAX ERROR directly
      ⍝ from Parser::collect_value_groups() (Parser.cc), before the
      ⍝ statement had an SI entry -- same failure mode as the unbalanced-
      ⍝ paren bug already fixed for Bugs27 #49, just for a BALANCED but
      ⍝ EMPTY pair instead. Symptom depended on context: at top level, the
      ⍝ raw throw got attributed to the PREVIOUS statement's SI instead of
      ⍝ this one; via ⍎, the caret display was lost entirely. Fixed the
      ⍝ same way as Bugs27 #49: an early, ErrorCode-returning pre-check in
      ⍝ Parser::parse_statement(), before any step that could throw raw.
      ⍝
      1+1
2
      ()
SYNTAX ERROR+

      ⍝ ⍎ now correctly shows the failed statement and carets (same as
      ⍝ any other ⍎-detected SYNTAX ERROR), instead of losing them.
      ⍝
      ⍎'()'
SYNTAX ERROR+
      ⍎'()'
      ^^

      ⍝ the failed ⍎ leaves a suspended SI entry, same as any other failed
      ⍝ execution (e.g. ⍎'1 2+') -- clear it before continuing.
      ⍝
      )SIC

      ⍝ same check for a few equivalent forms
      ⍝
      1()
SYNTAX ERROR+

      ( )
SYNTAX ERROR+

      ()+1
SYNTAX ERROR+

      A←()
SYNTAX ERROR+

      ⍝ ==================================
